# THE SHOPIFY CLI HONOURS THIS FILE ON PUSH. That is not obvious and it cost an
# hour: a gitignored snippet is never uploaded, and Liquid renders a MISSING
# snippet as empty with no error at all, so the page looks fine and the feature
# silently does not exist. Anything the theme needs at runtime must be un-ignored
# here, not just committed.
# The pulled stock theme is Shopify's, not mine, and most of its files would bury
# the two files that are. Only my additions, the perf work, the preview and the stock files noted in the README are tracked.
assets/*
!assets/spec-table.css
!assets/section-sale-event-hero.css
!assets/section-bundle-contents.css
!assets/sale-countdown.js
config/
locales/*
!locales/en.default.json
templates/*
!templates/product.json
!templates/page.sale-landing.json
!templates/collection.sale-event.json
sections/*
!sections/product-spec-table.liquid
!sections/main-product.liquid
!sections/sale-event-hero.liquid
!sections/bundle-contents.liquid
snippets/*
!snippets/seo-breadcrumb-jsonld.liquid
!snippets/spec-value.liquid
layout/
node_modules/
.shopify/
# app-cost output names the host it measured, so it is never tracked
perf/app-cost-*.json
